      <t:body>
         <t:listPlace>
            <t:place type="church dabr" subtype="institution">
               <t:placeName>Dabri Dabra Zakāryās Qǝddus Giyorgis</t:placeName>
               <t:placeName type="alt">Dabri Qǝddus Giyorgis</t:placeName>
               <t:country ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC3010Ethiop">Ethiopia</t:country>
               <t:region notBefore="1991" type="RegionalState" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC5932Tegray">Bǝḥerāwi Kǝllǝlāwi Mangǝśti Tǝgrāy</t:region>
               
               <t:settlement type="warada" from="2012-11-16" to="2012-12-04" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC3293GantaA">Gāntā ʾAfašum</t:settlement>  
               <t:settlement type="tabiya" from="2012-11-16" to="2012-12-04" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC7181Gwahgot">Gwāḥgot</t:settlement>
               
               <t:settlement from="2012-11-16" to="2012-12-04" type="qushat" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC7252Dabri">Dabri</t:settlement>
               
               <t:location>
                  <t:geo>14.141549 39.492582</t:geo>
                  <t:height unit="m">2587.96</t:height>
               </t:location>
               <t:note>
                  <t:date type="foundation" notBefore="1200" notAfter="1300">1200-1300</t:date>
                  <t:desc type="foundation">Local tradition claims that the church was founded in the time of King <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS4327GabraMa">Gabra Masqal</t:persName>, the tābot was brought by King <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS3729ellaAm">ʾAlʿāmedā</t:persName>.</t:desc>
                  <t:ab type="history">Dabr. Aksumite remains have been found in the vicinity. 
                     The recent church of <t:persName type="tabot" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS5684JesusCh#n3MadhaneAlam">Madḫāne ʿĀlam</t:persName> was built in the time of ; before,  (?).
The church of St. <t:persName type="tabot" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS4585Georgeo">George</t:persName> stands on the rock and is hardly accessible. 
                     The structures visible in the rock under the church of George (?) are said to have been a church dedicated to <t:persName type="tabot" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS3249Cyriacus">Qirqos</t:persName> (now deserted and inaccessible). 
                     In the valley, there is an associated church dedicated to <t:persName type="tabot" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS5684JesusCh#n3MadhaneAlam">Madḫāne ʿĀlam</t:persName>, built in <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS5226haylase">King Ḫāyla Śǝllāse</t:persName>'s time (<t:date>1930-1950</t:date>?; but it was founded by <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS6841MasasaW">
                        <t:roleName type="title">grāzmāč</t:roleName> Mašašā</t:persName>).  
</t:ab>
                  <t:ab type="description">
                     <t:figure>
                        <t:graphic url="Sites/DQG.tif">
                           <t:desc>The church photographed by Denis Nosnitsin during the Ethio-SPaRe project.</t:desc>
                        </t:graphic>
                     </t:figure>10 Mss. photographed: <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESdqg001">DQG-001</t:ref> “Miracles of Mary”; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESdqg002">DQG-002</t:ref> “Vita of Mar Giyorgis”; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESdqg003">DQG-003</t:ref> “Compilation of gospel's texts”; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESdqg004">DQG-004</t:ref> “Miracles of Mary”; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESdqg005">DQG-005</t:ref> “Vita of Giyorgis; Miracles of Giyorgis; Supplication prayer; Image of Giyorgis”; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESdqg006">DQG-006</t:ref> “Psalter”; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESdqg007">DQG-007</t:ref> “Harp of Praise”; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESdqg008">DQG-008</t:ref> “Four Gospels”; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESdqg009">DQG-009</t:ref> “Book of the Baptismal Ritual”; <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESdqg010">DQG-010</t:ref> “Praise of Marry”.</t:ab>
      
                  <t:ab type="tabot">
                     <t:measure quantity="3"/>Tābots of 2 of <t:persName type="tabot" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS4585Georgeo">George</t:persName> (in the upper church) and 1 <t:persName type="tabot" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS5684JesusCh#n3MadhaneAlam">Madḫāne ʿĀlam</t:persName> (below). 
                     The tābot of <t:persName type="tabot" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS3249Cyriacus">Qirqos</t:persName> is not there any more (reportedly stolen). The old dedication might be reflected in the name of the church, Dabra Zakāryās (<t:persName type="tabot" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS10692Zechari">Prophet Zechariah</t:persName>?).</t:ab>
               </t:note>
            </t:place>
         </t:listPlace>
